format session-log-v1
stamp 20260821.201333
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The guards run, and one of them had been quietly disarmed
prompt run the guards
think Ran all seventeen rather than the handful I expected to matter, because a guard nobody runs is indistinguishable from a guard that passes, and the whole day argued for asking rather than assuming.
think Two came back red, and both were mine from today, which is the honest result of a day spent building guards: the newest are the least exercised.
think Took the geode index first since it was obvious -- adding three tools this round moved the witness counts, so the generated page drifted from a fresh reading. That is the guard doing precisely its job, and regenerating is one command.
think Refused to guess at the dated-path failure and ran the resolver directly on the same case, which answered correctly. So the tool was fine and the witness was not, which is a much more interesting shape than a broken resolver.
think Replicated the witness's exact invocation from inside a Rishi script and got the right answer there too. That narrowed it to the witness's own bindings rather than anything it calls.
think Read the actual line and found it: folded_ref held the ALREADY-FOLDED path. The reference is supposed to be deliberately stale -- that is the whole point of it -- so the assert had been checking that an already-correct path resolves. True, and worthless.
think Found the culprit in one query rather than by reasoning. git log -S on the changed line named commit 0d31946c59, the repointer's own apply run. The tool rewrote the fixture that exists to prove the tool is needed.
think Saw the deeper fault immediately: the census already excluded dated_path_* by name, having learned this exact lesson hours earlier. The repointer, written the same day for the same corpus, never received the same exclusion -- so a lesson was recorded in one instrument and not carried to its sibling.
obs A green line is exactly what stops a person looking, which is why this survived several rounds that touched the tool. It only surfaced once the fixture's neighbours drifted enough to red the assert.
obs Three smaller findings from the same run, all illustrative rather than broken: a slice example in the new field guide used a real-looking dated filename as a literal, now placeholders per the mark law's own clause; two index rows I had shortened with an ellipsis read as broken paths, now written in full; and a control's planted page joined the census exclusions. lost fell 193 to 192 and the ceiling ratcheted down with it.
obs Owning one plainly: repairing those elided rows I typed a filename from memory, the-qoi-cleanroom-study, for a file actually named sel4-microkit-caravan-cleanroom-study. Caught by listing the directory a second later. A path written from memory is a path invented, every time.
loom guards=run total=17 green_first_pass=15 red=2 both_mine both_from_today
loom repair=fixture_restored culprit_commit=0d31946c59 found_by=git_log_dash_S
loom census=after gone=176 ambiguous=16 lost=192 ceiling=192 ratcheted_down_from=193
file tools/dated_path_witness.rish the stale fixture restored to the staleness it exists to prove
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_repoint_scan.sh the instrument's own fixtures excluded, as the census already did
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_scan.sh the control excluded; ceiling ratcheted 193 to 192
file docs-geode/api/rishi-language-reference.md the slice example illustrates with placeholders
file session-logs/README.md two elided filenames written in full, one of them corrected from an invention
file crux/REDS.md %121 -- a tool that edits its own fixtures disarms them silently
recommend check-in (checkpoint) all seventeen guards are GREEN, the disarmed one is armed again, and the lost-reference ceiling ratcheted down to 192. The honest note to carry: the two that failed were the two youngest, so the next cold start should run them before trusting them -- a guard earns confidence by being run, not by being written.
